<!--
  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Christopher Courtney <https://github.com/AES256Afro>
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the notarized macOS build.

  Notarization REQUIRES the hardened runtime signing option, which
  switches on protections that a CPython app packaged
  by PyInstaller trips over. Each entitlement below re-opens exactly one
  of them. Nothing here is speculative, and nothing grants network,
  camera, or file-access privileges.

  allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
      CPython allocates writable-then-executable memory for its own
      bytecode machinery, and several C extensions (notably libffi,
      which ctypes and cffi sit on) generate closures at runtime. Under
      the hardened runtime that is fatal at import time.

  disable-library-validation
      The bundle loads a large tree of third-party .dylibs and .so files
      that PyInstaller collected: OpenCV, Pillow, Tk, portaudio, plus
      the bundled ffmpeg/ffprobe binaries. Library validation demands
      every loaded library be signed by the *same* Team ID; these are
      re-signed by the build, but validation still rejects loading them
      from a Resources subtree, so it has to be off.

  Deliberately NOT granted: allow-dyld-environment-variables and
  debugger entitlements. Neither is needed and both weaken the build.
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
